  "question": {
    "text": "A wheel is rotating at $900 \\mathrm{r}$.p.m. about its axis. When power is cut offit comes to rest in 1 minute. The angular retardation in $\\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}^{2}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\pi / 2$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\pi / 4$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\pi / 6$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\pi / 8$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Angular retardation,\r\n\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\alpha &=\\frac{\\omega_{2}-\\omega_{1}}{t}=\\frac{2 \\pi\\left(\\mathrm{n}_{2}-\\mathrm{n}_{1}\\right)}{\\mathrm{t}} \\\\ &=\\frac{2 \\pi(0-900 / 60)}{60}=\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}^{2} \\end{aligned}$"
  }
}